law.text:
		Any officer, director, employee, receiver, or agent of a credit union who willfully does any of the following is guilty of a Class 6 felony:

With the intent to deceive, falsifies any book of account, report, statement, record, or other document of a credit union, whether by alteration, false entry, omission, or otherwise;


Signs, issues, publishes, or transmits to a government agency any book of account, report, statement, record, or other document that he knows to be false;


By means of deceit, obtains a signature to a writing that is a subject of forgery;


With intent to deceive, destroys any credit union book of account, report, statement, record, or other document; or


With the intent to defraud, shares or receives directly or indirectly any money, property, or benefits through any transaction of the credit union.
